   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "decimal place",
     "divisor",
     "shift the point"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "To multiply decimals, ignore the points and multiply as whole numbers, then put the point so that the answer has as many decimal places as both numbers together. 1.2 x 0.3 is 12 x 3 = 36 with 2 places, so 0.36.\nTo divide by a decimal, multiply both numbers by 10 until the divisor is whole. 4.5 divided by 0.5 is 45 divided by 5, which is 9.\nMultiplying by 10, 100, 1000 moves the point to the right."
    }
